        "answerKey": "1. Definition: A set U in R^n is open if for every point x in U, there exists an epsilon > 0 such that the open ball B(x, epsilon) is contained in U.\n2. Proof for B(a, r):\n   Let x be any point in B(a, r). Thus, d = \\|x - a\\| < r.\n   Choose epsilon = r - d > 0.\n3. Let y be any point in B(x, epsilon). By the triangle inequality:\n   \\|y - a\\| \\le \\|y - x\\| + \\|x - a\\| < epsilon + d = (r - d) + d = r.\n   Thus, y is in B(a, r).\n4. This shows that B(x, epsilon) is contained in B(a, r). Hence, B(a, r) is open."
