        "answerKey": "1. Concept: The tangent space Tp(R^n) at a point p in R^n is the vector space consisting of all tangent vectors at p. It can be viewed as the space of all velocity vectors of smooth curves passing through p, or as the space of derivations at p.\n2. Dimension: The dimension of Tp(R^n) is n, matching the dimension of the underlying Euclidean space.\n3. Basis: Under the derivation viewpoint, the standard basis elements are represented by the partial differential operators: e_i = \\partial/\\partial x_i evaluated at p, for i = 1, 2, ..., n.\n4. Any vector v in Tp(R^n) can be written as the linear combination: v = \\sum v_i (\\partial/\\partial x_i)|_p."
