        "answerKey": "1. Let f1(r, theta) = r cos(theta) and f2(r, theta) = r sin(theta).\n2. The Jacobian matrix J consists of partial derivatives:\n   J = [\n     [ \\partial f1/\\partial r, \\partial f1/\\partial \\theta ],\n     [ \\partial f2/\\partial r, \\partial f2/\\partial \\theta ]\n   ]\n3. Compute derivatives:\n   \\partial f1/\\partial r = cos(theta), \\partial f1/\\partial \\theta = -r sin(theta)\n   \\partial f2/\\partial r = sin(theta), \\partial f2/\\partial \\theta = r cos(theta)\n4. Write the matrix:\n   J = [\n     [ cos(theta), -r sin(theta) ],\n     [ sin(theta),  r cos(theta) ]\n   ]\n5. Determinant: det(J) = cos(theta) * (r cos(theta)) - (-r sin(theta)) * sin(theta) = r cos^2(theta) + r sin^2(theta) = r."
