        "answerKey": "1. Theorem: Let f: U in R^n -> R^n be continuously differentiable on open set U. If det J_f(a) != 0 at point a in U, then:\n   - There exists an open neighborhood V containing a, and open neighborhood W containing f(a), such that f: V -> W is a bijection.\n   - The inverse function f^(-1): W -> V is continuously differentiable, and its derivative is given by: J_{f^(-1)}(f(a)) = [J_f(a)]^(-1).\n2. Significance of det J_f(a) != 0:\n   This condition guarantees that the linear approximation of f at point a is invertible. Geometrically, it ensures f is locally one-to-one and has a well-defined local inverse."
