        "answerKey": "1. Let (x0, y0) be a critical point of f(x,y), i.e. fx(x0,y0) = 0 and fy(x0,y0) = 0.\n2. Construct the Hessian determinant D (or discriminant):\n   D = fxx(x0,y0) * fyy(x0,y0) - [fxy(x0,y0)]^2.\n3. Local Minimum: If D > 0 and fxx(x0,y0) > 0.\n4. Local Maximum: If D > 0 and fxx(x0,y0) < 0.\n5. Saddle Point: If D < 0. (The function has positive and negative curvatures).\n6. Inconclusive Test: If D = 0. Further analysis is required."
