        "question": "State Dirichlet's Integral Formula for evaluation of multiple integrals. Use it to find the volume of the region bounded by $x \\ge 0, y \\ge 0, z \\ge 0$ and $x + y + z \\le 1$.",
        "answerKey": "1. Dirichlet's Formula: \\iiint_V x^{l-1} y^{m-1} z^{n-1} dx dy dz = [Gamma(l)Gamma(m)Gamma(n)] / Gamma(l + m + n + 1) for x,y,z >= 0, x+y+z <= 1.\n2. Volume integral: V = \\iiint_V 1 dx dy dz.\n3. Match exponents: l-1 = 0 => l = 1, m-1 = 0 => m = 1, n-1 = 0 => n = 1.\n4. Apply formula:\n   V = [Gamma(1)Gamma(1)Gamma(1)] / Gamma(1 + 1 + 1 + 1) = [1 * 1 * 1] / Gamma(4).\n5. Compute Gamma(4) = 3! = 6.\n6. Volume V = 1/6."
