        "answerKey": "1. Liouville's Theorem: If V is bounded by x,y,z >= 0 and h1 <= x+y+z <= h2, then:\n   \\iiint_V x^{l-1} y^{m-1} z^{n-1} f(x+y+z) dx dy dz = [Gamma(l)Gamma(m)Gamma(n)/Gamma(l+m+n)] * \\int_{h1}^{h2} h^{l+m+n-1} f(h) dh.\n2. Match exponents: l=1, m=1, n=1. Function f(u) = sqrt(u). Bounds: h1 = 0, h2 = 1.\n3. Coefficient: [Gamma(1)Gamma(1)Gamma(1) / Gamma(3)] = 1/2! = 1/2.\n4. Evaluate integral w.r.t h:\n   \\int_0^1 h^{1+1+1-1} sqrt(h) dh = \\int_0^1 h^2 * h^{1/2} dh = \\int_0^1 h^{5/2} dh = [2/7 h^{7/2}]_0^1 = 2/7.\n5. Multiply: (1/2) * (2/7) = 1/7."
