        "answerKey": "1. Stokes' Theorem: $\\iint_S (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{F})\\cdot d\\mathbf{S} = \\oint_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot d\\mathbf{r}$, where $C$ is the boundary of $S$.\n2. Boundary $C$: the unit circle $x^2+y^2=1$, $z=0$, traversed counterclockwise.\n3. Parametrize: $x=\\cos t$, $y=\\sin t$, $z=0$, $t\\in[0,2\\pi]$.\n4. $\\mathbf{F}|_C = \\sin t\\,\\hat{i} - \\cos t\\,\\hat{j} + 0$; $d\\mathbf{r} = (-\\sin t\\,\\hat{i}+\\cos t\\,\\hat{j})dt$.\n5. $\\oint_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot d\\mathbf{r} = \\int_0^{2\\pi}(\\sin t(-\\sin t) + (-\\cos t)(\\cos t))dt = \\int_0^{2\\pi}(-\\sin^2 t - \\cos^2 t)dt = \\int_0^{2\\pi}(-1)dt = -2\\pi$."
