        "topic": "Curvilinear Coordinates",
        "question": "Derive the divergence of a vector field $\\mathbf{A} = A_1\\hat{e}_1 + A_2\\hat{e}_2 + A_3\\hat{e}_3$ in general orthogonal curvilinear coordinates with scale factors $h_1, h_2, h_3$.",
        "answerKey": "1. The divergence in curvilinear coords is: $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf{A} = \\frac{1}{h_1 h_2 h_3}\\left[\\frac{\\partial(h_2 h_3 A_1)}{\\partial q_1} + \\frac{\\partial(h_1 h_3 A_2)}{\\partial q_2} + \\frac{\\partial(h_1 h_2 A_3)}{\\partial q_3}\\right]$.\n2. Derivation: Use Gauss's theorem on an infinitesimal volume element $dV = h_1 h_2 h_3\\,dq_1\\,dq_2\\,dq_3$.\n3. The flux through the face at $q_1 + dq_1$: $A_1 h_2 h_3\\,dq_2\\,dq_3$ evaluated at $q_1+dq_1$.\n4. Net flux through $q_1$ faces: $\\frac{\\partial(h_2 h_3 A_1)}{\\partial q_1}dq_1\\,dq_2\\,dq_3$. Similarly for the other pairs.\n5. Dividing by $dV$: gives the formula above. For cylindrical: $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf{A} = \\frac{1}{\\rho}\\frac{\\partial(\\rho A_\\rho)}{\\partial\\rho} + \\frac{1}{\\rho}\\frac{\\partial A_\\phi}{\\partial\\phi} + \\frac{\\partial A_z}{\\partial z}$."
